# Delphine's Thread of Fate at camp (Ascendancy): the beats that wait for a rest (story/camp_talk.gd offers the first `talk_` node whose opening `if` holds,
# once a playthrough). Order matters: the Incitement's echo, the Discovery, the Confrontation (held back while Delphine is Strained until the
# `talk_confrontation_wait` word has been had, never for good). Rewards come from Fateweaving when each beat's quest ends (story/fateweaving.gd).
# Drafted by Gemini (docs/plans/gemini_companions/), edited; every edit is listed in the README there. Lines are unvoiced until the voice lane reads them.

~ talk_incitement
if name:delphine_ravelle and flag.pending_ascendancy_incitement and not flag.incitement_ascendancy
-> incitement
endif
-> END

~ incitement
Narrator: Delphine sits near the coals with her ink-stained notebook open on her knee, flattenin' a damp scrap of paper that smells of sour paste.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: I slipped back to that drafty circus car before we left the wreck behind, darlings.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Some poor ghost was still tumbling from the rafters while this old handbill rotted on the wall.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: I peeled it down and copied the border of crowns and bells right into my lining.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: The whole time my needle moved, Your Foolishness hummed a three-note fanfare over my shoulder without cracking a single joke.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Every stitch in my back was sewn for a ring like the one on that poster.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: When a jester stops laughing at the billing, the curtain is about to drop on somebody's neck.
* Show us what you copied from the poster. -> incitement_1
* Keep your notes dry. We have a long road ahead. -> incitement_2

~ incitement_1
Narrator: Delphine tilts the page toward the firelight, tracing the sketched crowns with a needle-scarred thumb.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Stick by me when we reach the big tents, and I will see that you get the finest seats in the house.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Once I untangle his cue sheet, nobody will ever pull our strings again.
set incitement_ascendancy
quest connection_ascendancy waiting
set delphine_inc_choice = "shared"
inspire name:delphine_ravelle: met the Fool's silence over a handbill
-> END

~ incitement_2
Narrator: Delphine snaps the notebook shut and slips it neatly behind her velvet lapel.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: A wise headliner knows how to rehearse her lines in the dark. Come morning, I will be ready for whatever stage this hollow builds.
set incitement_ascendancy
quest connection_ascendancy waiting
set delphine_inc_choice = "alone"
inspire name:delphine_ravelle: met the Fool's silence over a handbill
-> END

~ talk_discovery
if name:delphine_ravelle and flag.connection_ascendancy and flag.renathyr_slain and not flag.discovery_ascendancy
-> discovery
endif
-> END

~ discovery
Narrator: Delphine holds her open notebook close to the flames, rubbing a smudge of black ink from her thumb while the air above her left shoulder stays dead still.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Mind the seams, darling, because the air in the Crimson Monastery nearly ruined my best velvet.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Still, the trip paid off, because I finally caught Your Foolishness with his mouth shut.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: He has been rattling off crooked verses in my ear since the first night we met, daring me to guess the punchline.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Up in those cold rafters, the pieces of his riddle finally fell into place on the bias.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: I spoke the answer right out loud to the empty room, expecting him to cackle or spin a cartwheel.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Instead, the old head just went quiet, and he has not laughed once since we walked back down.
Narrator: She taps her silver scissors against her knee, her glass button eye fixed on the curl of smoke rising from the logs.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: You would think winning the round would feel like top billing on opening night.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: That is the whole bargain, after all, solving his puzzles until I am stitched tight enough that no hand can unpick me.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Yet when the answer left my tongue, it did not sound like one of his carnival tricks at all.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: It sounded like an old debt being called in from the back of the house.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: I spent all evening checking the margin notes, and the rest of the page is still waiting for ink.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: If he knows the whole song already, I am starting to wonder who actually wrote my part.
* What did the answer sound like to you? -> discovery_1
* Whatever the part is, you will make the stage yours. -> discovery_2
* At least he is quiet tonight. Get some rest. -> discovery_3

~ discovery_1
Narrator: Delphine lowers her voice to a papery hush, her thumb smoothing the frayed edge of her cuff.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Like a cue I heard once from the wings, back before I knew what the price of a spotlight really was.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: That is quite enough ancient history for one campfire, so let the embers take it.
approve delphine_ravelle +2: You asked what the riddle's answer sounded like to me.
set discovery_ascendancy
quest discovery_ascendancy done
quest confrontation_ascendancy waiting
-> END

~ discovery_2
Narrator: A quick, brassy grin returns to Delphine's face as she tucks the scissors into her sash.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Spoken like a true patron of the arts, and do not think I will forget it when my name is on the marquee.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: No matter who drafted the script, I am the one taking the bow.
approve delphine_ravelle +3: You backed my claim to the stage after the Crimson Monastery.
set discovery_ascendancy
quest discovery_ascendancy done
quest confrontation_ascendancy waiting
-> END

~ discovery_3
Narrator: Delphine closes her book with a dry snap and brushes a speck of ash from her skirt.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Silence from the prompter's box is a rare treat, I will grant you that much. Sleep tight in the cheap seats, the show is far from settled.
approve delphine_ravelle -1: You left me to my quiet after the Crimson Monastery.
set discovery_ascendancy
quest discovery_ascendancy done
quest confrontation_ascendancy waiting
-> END

~ talk_confrontation_wait
if name:delphine_ravelle and flag.discovery_ascendancy and flag.chuckles_dead and not flag.confrontation_ascendancy and approval.delphine_ravelle <= strained and not flag.delphine_ravelle_confrontation_waited
-> confrontation_wait
endif
-> END

~ confrontation_wait
Narrator: Delphine sits apart on a dry crate, pullin' a length of red thread through her cuff with brisk, brittle jerks of her wrist.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Before you ask about Fool's Day, darling, save your breath for the fire.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: I took a turn on that stage worth a whole chapter in the ledger, and the ink is staying locked in my lining tonight.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: I signed on to travel with headliners who had some flair in their boots and some respect for a proper act.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Lately our little company has been marching like joyless bailiffs who think every piece of work around them is spare parts.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: A grand turn deserves a warm house, not a cold shoulder in the wings. Until we find our rhythm again, my best material stays behind the curtain.
* We have been careless lately. We will do better by you. -> confrontation_wait_1
* Keep your story to yourself, then. We have work to do. -> confrontation_wait_2
* Say nothing. Stay by the fire. -> confrontation_wait_3

~ confrontation_wait_1
Narrator: Delphine pauses with her needle in the felt, the tight line of her shoulders easing by a fraction.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: See that you do, because a shabby chorus ruins the finest solo in the province.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Show me some style on the road tomorrow, and perhaps we will open the book again.
approve delphine_ravelle +6: You owned your missteps when our company felt strained.
set delphine_ravelle_confrontation_waited
-> END

~ confrontation_wait_2
Narrator: Delphine bites the red thread off clean and turns her button eye back to the dark trees.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Spoken like a true usher slamming the doors before the overture is even finished. When you remember how to treat a star, you know where my campstool is.
approve delphine_ravelle -2: You told me to keep my story to myself.
set delphine_ravelle_confrontation_waited
-> END

~ confrontation_wait_3
Narrator: Delphine ties off her knot in silence, lets the firelight warm her stitched hands, and does not move away when you stay.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: At least you know how to hold a quiet cue without trampling the hem.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Give it a night or two, and we will see how the house lights look.
set delphine_ravelle_confrontation_waited
-> END

~ talk_confrontation
if name:delphine_ravelle and flag.discovery_ascendancy and flag.chuckles_dead and not flag.confrontation_ascendancy and (approval.delphine_ravelle > strained or flag.delphine_ravelle_confrontation_waited)
-> confrontation
endif
-> END

~ confrontation
Narrator: Delphine stands by the fire with her coat unbuttoned at the collar, turnin' her worn notebook over in her hands without opening the cover.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Well, Fool's Day certainly lived up to the handbill, and my ears are still ringing from the noise.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Your Foolishness thought he was going to take the center ring for himself and leave me holding the prompt book.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: He rolled out the last of his grand rhyme right there under the lights, waiting for me to trip over the meter.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Everything I ran from when I first stitched my own hem was waiting in that verse, dressed up like a royal promise.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: He wanted me to step into the final measure just the way it was written, neat and cold and untouchable.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: For a heartbeat, looking at the crowd, I almost took the cue he handed me.
Narrator: She sets the closed notebook down on the log beside you, her fingers steady on the leather spine.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Then I heard how lonely the rhythm was, and I decided I had taken quite enough direction from a floating head without a jawbone.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: I stepped right across his mark, took the stage away from him, and spoke my own ending over his rhyme.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: He says you're lying, and he doesn't even have eyes, or at least that used to be his favorite little barb.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Tonight he did not have a single word left to throw at my back.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: The funny thing is, I am still made of the exact same felt and thread I wore yesterday morning.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: No magic needle came down from the rafters to make me seamless.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: I wrote the finish myself, and the curtain is still up.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Tell me the truth by the firelight, does a patchwork girl look any different when she owns her own billing?
* What were the words you put at the end of his rhyme? -> confrontation_1
* You look like a headliner who needs no strings at all. -> confrontation_2
* The festival is behind us now. Let the curtain come down. -> confrontation_3

~ confrontation_1
Narrator: Delphine taps her chest right over her ribs, her voice dropping into a warm, quiet register.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Just a plain line stating that a seam you mend yourself holds stronger than any crown borrowed from a ghost.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: It may not scan for the gallery, yet it was the first true verse I ever spoke.
approve delphine_ravelle +4: You asked for the words I spoke on Fool's Day.
set confrontation_ascendancy
quest confrontation_ascendancy done
-> END

~ confrontation_2
Narrator: Delphine sweeps you a low cabaret bow by the embers, her glass button eye bright as polished brass.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Put that in the papers, and print it in letters tall enough to read from the cheap seats.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: As long as this company shares the bill, I do not mind a few rough stitches showing.
approve delphine_ravelle +6: You called me a headliner with no strings after Fool's Day.
set confrontation_ascendancy
quest confrontation_ascendancy done
-> END

~ confrontation_3
Narrator: Delphine picks up her notebook and slips it back into her lining with an easy shrug.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Fair enough, even the loudest carnival has to pack the wagons before dawn. The rhyme is finished on my terms, and that is plenty to sleep on.
approve delphine_ravelle -2: You told me to let the curtain come down after Fool's Day.
set confrontation_ascendancy
quest confrontation_ascendancy done
-> END
